course: dictionary
lesson: 12850
title: Endowed: gifts and money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Endowed» can mean two things, so read the words around it to find which one fits. «Maya was endowed with great patience.» Patience is a good quality, and endowed with means she naturally has it. You could say "born with" instead, and the sentence would still make sense.
explain: «The old school was endowed by a rich woman in 1850.» Here endowed means that someone gave the school a large sum of money, and that money keeps paying for the school. The clues are school and rich woman, and the thing given is money, not a quality.
explain: Endowed is a formal, old-fashioned word, so you will mostly meet it in books and history lessons. When a word is new, swap in a simple meaning and check the sentence. If it still does not make sense, use a dictionary.
fact: Endowed means given something, often a quality, an ability or money.
fact: If a person is endowed with something, they naturally have a good quality or ability, such as «endowed with great patience».
fact: If a school, hospital or college is endowed, someone has given it a large sum of money that keeps paying for it.
fact: The US Declaration of Independence says people are «endowed by their Creator with certain unalienable Rights».
fact: Endowed is an old-fashioned or formal word, so you will meet it mostly in books and history.
exercise: «Nature had endowed her with a quick mind.» What does endowed with mean here? | *Naturally had as a gift | Bought a new car | Lost, as in lost her way | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The hospital was endowed by a kind banker, so it still has money to pay its doctors.» What does endowed mean here? | Closed down for repairs | *Given a large sum of money that keeps paying for it | Made smaller in size | Painted white and blue
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells you someone gave the college money: «The college is well endowed, and it has a library full of books.» | *endowed | library | books | college
test: «The children were endowed with a kind heart.» What does endowed with mean? | *Naturally had a kind heart | Lost their kind hearts | Painted a kind picture | Were tired of a kind heart
test: «The old chapel was endowed by a rich family long ago, so it still has money to pay for repairs.» Why does the chapel still have money? | It was painted with gold | It was built only last year | The family borrowed money from it | *Someone gave it a large sum that keeps paying
exam: «Her teacher said she was endowed with a gift for music.» What does endowed with mean? | *Naturally has a gift for music | Lost her music book | Sold her piano | Is tired of music
